A formatter for Python code.

YAPF (Yet Another Python Formatter) is based on the algorithm of
clang-format: it reformats code to the layout that best conforms to the
configured style, rather than only fixing style-guide violations.
Predefined styles include pep8, google, facebook and yapf, and options can
be set in setup.cfg, pyproject.toml or a .style.yapf file.  It can be used
as a command-line tool or as a library.
